Directories:

COMMON: ELAN files used by both the interpreted and compiled versions

ARITY_N_C: ELAN files used by the compiled  version

ARITY_N_I: ELAN files used by the interpreted version

DEMO: Some examples


The directories ARITY_N_C and ARITY_N_I have the following structure:

src: The sources files (ELAN files).


To install COLETTE:

Add the path to the directory containing COLETTE.

Define the variable COLETTE as the directory containing COLETTE.


To use COLETTE:

colette arity version strategy_name spc_file trace_option query_file


where:

arity must be N (eventually 2.)


version can be I or C for the interpreted or compiled version, respectively.


strategy_name must be one of the strategy names included in the ELAN files.


spc_file must be a file name including the specification you want to use. In 
the spc directory there are some example files.


trace_option specifies the trace level and must be:

b to run COLETTE in a batch mode
q to run COLETTE in a quiet mode
't n' to run COLETTE with trace level 'n'


query_file must be a file name containing the query (only used for the 
compiled version)


For more information you can visit COLETTE Home Page:

http://www.loria.fr/~castro/COLETTE/index.html


